{"id": "tea:siva-svarodaya:topic.actions", "source": "src:siva-svarodaya", "location": {"ref": "topic.actions"}, "paraphrase": "Steady and auspicious acts are to be done when the moon (left) flows, active and harsh acts when the sun (right) flows; when suṣumnā flows, worldly acts fail and only meditation and yoga should be done.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "world-fate"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "concepts": ["cpt:svara-science"], "practices": ["prc:svara-yoga"], "speaker": "Śiva", "addressee": "Pārvatī", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:siva-svarodaya:topic.death-signs", "source": "src:siva-svarodaya", "location": {"ref": "topic.death-signs"}, "paraphrase": "The flow of the breath is used to foretell events — success, illness, the outcome of battles — and the approach of death.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["death-dying", "world-fate"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "concepts": ["cpt:death-omens", "cpt:svara-science"], "speaker": "Śiva", "addressee": "Pārvatī", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:siva-svarodaya:topic.five-tattvas", "source": "src:siva-svarodaya", "location": {"ref": "topic.five-tattvas"}, "paraphrase": "In each flow the five elements (earth, water, fire, air, space) arise in turn, known by the length, direction, colour and taste of the breath.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "concepts": ["cpt:five-tattvas-in-breath", "cpt:svara-science"], "terms": ["trm:tattva"], "speaker": "Śiva", "addressee": "Pārvatī", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:siva-svarodaya:topic.three-flows", "source": "src:siva-svarodaya", "location": {"ref": "topic.three-flows"}, "paraphrase": "The breath flows through iḍā (left, moon), piṅgalā (right, sun) or suṣumnā (both); the flows alternate through the day in a regular order; the knowledge of svara is the most secret of sciences.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "concepts": ["cpt:svara-science", "cpt:sun-moon-fire"], "terms": ["trm:svara", "trm:ida", "trm:pingala", "trm:susumna"], "speaker": "Śiva", "addressee": "Pārvatī", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
